      en: "The National Abattoir, located in the Khubetsoana area of Maseru, is a critical infrastructure component for Lesotho's livestock sector. Designed to centralize meat processing, the facility ensures that beef and mutton production meets national hygiene and safety standards. Most of the animals processed here are sourced from local Basotho farmers who graze their herds in the highland pastures. As a government-regulated entity, it plays a vital role in national food security by providing a reliable supply of meat to urban centers and reducing reliance on imports from neighboring South Africa. The complex also serves as an economic hub, supporting the livelihoods of rural communities by offering a guaranteed market for their livestock. Beyond slaughtering, the site is instrumental in maintaining quality control within the domestic food chain and supporting the growth of the local agribusiness industry.",
